WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:07.610
Speaker 1: . Now, let's talk about one statistic
in the U.S. that is pandemic related, that

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:13.330
is really not looking very good, and that
is that hospitalizations in the United States

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:18.779
are rising, not overall, but in areas with
low vaccination rates.

00:00:18.779 --> 00:00:24.269
Now, we've been talking for months at this
point in time, if 20 percent of the country

00:00:24.269 --> 00:00:28.609
never gets vaccinated, which the latest polling
we have is that 20 percent of the country

00:00:28.609 --> 00:00:31.079
does not plan to get the coronavirus vaccine.

00:00:31.079 --> 00:00:32.079
What's going to happen?

00:00:32.079 --> 00:00:34.410
Well, we'll never eradicate it fully.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:35.629
We may never anyway.

00:00:35.629 --> 00:00:41.160
But in addition to not eradicating it fully,
you're going to see these clusters pop up

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:46.239
in the areas that have a lower percentage
of the population vaccinated.

00:00:46.239 --> 00:00:52.129
And statistically speaking, most of the people
who get it will be the unvaccinated.

00:00:52.129 --> 00:00:54.339
But the vaccines aren't 100 percent effective.

00:00:54.339 --> 00:00:59.089
When we say 94, 95 percent, that means roughly
one out of 20 people who get vaccinated do

00:00:59.089 --> 00:01:00.610
not develop antibodies.

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:07.850
So these unvaccinated areas will also lead
to some vaccinated people getting sick.

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:11.870
And statistically, if enough of them get sick,
some of those people are going to die.

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:13.490
This is happening now.

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:16.890
We had the idea maybe that would be at the
end of summer, maybe into the fall or winter,

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:19.030
where you would start to see these clusters.

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:20.420
They're happening now.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:26.810
There's a new New York Times report which
says in the U.S., hospitalizations are rising

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:28.850
in areas with low vaccination rates.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:35.250
Health officials worry that covid-19 hospitalization
rates could increase among the unvaccinated

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:37.840
as variants of the virus spread.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:42.490
The coronavirus might be receding in much
of the U.S., this article writes, but it continues

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:47.530
to spread in communities with low covid vaccination
rates, where highly contagious virus variants

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:50.840
pose a threat to those who have not had shots.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:54.869
As an example, the article mentions Smith
County, Tennessee.

00:01:54.869 --> 00:01:59.340
Only 20 percent of the population in Smith
County, Tennessee, are fully vaccinated, and

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:07.100
there has been a 700 percent increase in hospitalizations
for covid and 19 over the last two weeks,

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.690
according to the New York Times database.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:16.700
Another example in Truesdale, Tennessee, or
maybe it's pronounced Truesdale, a 23 percent

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:23.260
of the population is fully vaccinated, hospitalizations
up 700 percent.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.170
This is not a coincidence.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:34.790
Dr. Ted Delbridge says in most age groups,
people who become ill are twice as likely

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:39.220
to end up hospitalized as people who got the
virus earlier in the pandemic.

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:40.220
What does this mean?

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:45.130
This means that these variants are not only
more contagious, but more likely to make you

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:46.920
sick if you are not vaccinated.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:53.040
So all else being equal, if you have 50 percent
of the population unvaccinated now versus

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:58.290
at some previous point now, more likely people
are going to get really sick and sick enough

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:02.340
to get hospitalized because of these variants
in Maryland.

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:07.980
Of those between 50 and 59 years of age who
got covid over the winter, eight percent were

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:15.280
hospitalized from April April on, 19 percent
of people in that age group who got the virus

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:17.030
were hospitalized.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.860
And the vaccines protect you.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:21.810
This is not going to stop.

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:24.680
This is not going to go away in this way.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:32.340
And I know that there's a lot of tough talk
about I'm healthy, I eat a good diet, I exercise,

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:36.750
et cetera, that doesn't protect you from covid-19.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:43.460
And as the variants that that are predominant
are more transmissible and or more likely

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:47.020
to put you in the hospital, you are taking
a real big.

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:50.840
Risk by being unvaccinated, but you were also
putting other people at risk at this point,

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:51.840
it's like a broken record.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:57.900
I don't know how many times it has to be said
the vaccines are effective against the variants.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:02.210
They are slightly less effective against some
of the most recent variants.

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:09.090
But you get really good protection from all
known variants so far if you just go and get

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:10.150
vaccinated.

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:12.550
And so we talked earlier about the numbers.

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:15.620
We're now down to about 14000 cases per day.

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:20.959
It's it's really quite low, some of the lowest
we've been at for for a while.

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:22.650
Where do we go from here?

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:26.919
Where do we go from here if we continue to
see this vaccine hesitancy?

00:04:26.919 --> 00:04:30.169
So a little bit later, we're going to talk
about Biden's infrastructure negotiations

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:31.169
and some other things.

00:04:31.169 --> 00:04:36.919
Later, we're going to actually have video
from a hearing where attendees were arguing

00:04:36.919 --> 00:04:40.849
against any kind of required vaccination.

00:04:40.849 --> 00:04:43.909
And the nuttery is growing significantly.

00:04:43.909 --> 00:04:45.730
The nuttery is spreading like a virus.

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:47.599
So we're going to talk about that later.

00:04:47.599 --> 00:04:50.830
We're going to talk about lab week, but send
me your thoughts.

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:57.979
How low do you think cases can go if 20 percent
of the population really refuses to get themselves

00:04:57.979 --> 00:04:58.979
vaccinated?

